meta {
  name: Get team panel
  type: http
  seq: 1
}

get {
  url: {{baseUrl}}/practices/:practiceId/teams/1
  body: none
  auth: none
}

params:path {
  practiceId: 1
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 200
}

docs {
  The fragment behind the team tabs on the practice page.
  
  ## Edge cases
  
  | URL change | Expected |
  |---|---|
  | `/teams/2` | the other team |
  | `/teams/3` or `/teams/0` | `400`, empty body |
  | `/teams/kissa` | `400`, empty body |
  | practice `999999` | `200`, an EMPTY team panel |
  
  This handler validates the range explicitly
  (`teamNumber < 1 || teamNumber > 2`) and returns a bare `400` with no
  body. HTMX drops 4xx bodies by default, so nothing is swapped and the
  page is unchanged.
  
  A practice that doesn't exist is not an error here:
  `GetPracticeTeamPlayers` returns an empty slice, so you get a panel with
  zero players and a `200`. The practice PAGE (`GET /practices/{id}`)
  404s for the same id.
}
